   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the period during which\nthe county of Orleans is authorized to impose additional rates of sales and\ncompensating use taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S5561",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5561-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5561\n\nSPONSOR: ORTT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the period during\nwhich the county of Orleans is authorized to impose additional rates of\nsales and compensating use taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would extend the sales and compensating use tax in the\ncounty of Orleans.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection lestablishes the sales and compensating tax rate, which is an\nadditional 1% to the 3% rate authorized, is extended to 2027.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe county of Orleans requires legislation to extend the expiration of\nthe imposition of an additional 1% sales and compensating use tax which\nexpires November 30, 2025.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
